        }
      ],
      "words": 70
    },
    {
      "block": "原句6",
      "no": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "She had worried herself sick over this day. Now she looked like she had been born for it",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6292
        },
        {
          "text": "Carson told her yes",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6659
        },
        {
          "text": "Which wasn’t remotely true, but I imagined a younger Carson who thought the same thing. The image brought a smile to my ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6680
        },
        {
          "text": "I laughed, shaking my head, because Carson was never one to ruin someone’s dream",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6946
        }
      ],
      "words": 62
    },
    {
      "block": "原句7",
      "no": 7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "I had spent the last month thinking I was falling",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7602
        },
        {
          "text": "Somewhere between the first hayride and her threatening to murder Rosie over a missing box of extension cords, I realize",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7669
        },
        {
          "text": "no falling left",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7816
        },
        {
          "text": "I loved everything about her already",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7839
        }
      ],
      "words": 45
    },
    {
      "block": "原句8",
      "no": 8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "I loved the woman who walked into my garage, soaked through and furious",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 8323
        },
        {
          "text": "I loved the girl I’d watched race Blueberry in old videos",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 8396
        },
        {
          "text": "I loved the granddaughter who still carried Pops around",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 8454
        },
        {
          "text": "I loved the rancher who knew which cow was sick before anyone else",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 8537
        },
        {
          "text": "I loved the woman who had spent years believing half her body",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 8605
        },
        {
          "text": "And maybe most terrifying of all, I loved the future version of Carson I didn’t know yet",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 8715
        },
        {
          "text": "The one she was still becoming",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 8804
        }
      ],
      "words": 87
    },
    {
      "block": "原句9",
      "no": 9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“You love her.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9149
        },
        {
          "text": "“You fucking love her.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9180
        },
        {
          "text": "“Say it louder.” I grabbed the extension cord beside me. “I think somebody in Alabama missed it.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9202
        },
        {
          "text": "Jax’s grin disappeared. “Saved by the devil.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9393
        },
        {
          "text": "“You seem to spend a lot of time with that devil.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9436
        }
      ],
      "words": 46
    },
    {
      "block": "原句10",
      "no": 10,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Around one, I noticed Carson’s limp getting worse. Nobody else seemed to catch it. Yet I did, because I was watching for",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9524
        },
        {
          "text": "She was near the cider booth reviewing something with Meme",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9768
        },
        {
          "text": "I walked past them toward Sugar and Pine",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9828
        },
        {
          "text": "“Want your usual, sweetheart?”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 10031
        },
        {
          "text": "Ten minutes later, I found her sitting on the open tailgate of Dad’s truck near the barn, eating the sandwich I’d brough",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 10115
        },
        {
          "text": "Carson looked at me after a minute. “I know what you did.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 10299
        },
        {
          "text": "“You’re still bossy.” Her knee bumped my arm",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 10429
        }
      ],
      "words": 98
    },
    {
      "block": "原句11",
      "no": 11,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "As if we had summoned her, Carson appeared in the doorway. My eyes went to her face first. Then lower. Her prosthetic le",
          "ok": true,
